WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.590
Magical flying hammers may make for great
weapons in the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:08.380
but according to Chris Hemsworth's wife, they
don't make for great house decor.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:13.570
Most actors like to take home a piece of memorabilia
from the sets of their films like small props

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:17.470
or a piece of clothing to remind them of a
special time in their life or an important

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:18.380
character they played.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.720
If you're the God of Thunder, however, your
eyes are firmly affixed on your faithful hammer,

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:23.220
Mjolnir.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.060
“Myeu Muh?

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:25.420
What's Myeu Muh?”

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.720
Thor, whom Hemsworth has played in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe since the release of…

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.480
well, Thor in 2011, is known to wield Mjolnir
at all times in combat, making frequent use

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.440
of a deadly swing that could knock even the
Hulk out of his boots if the green monster

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:40.400
wore any, of course.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.570
The enchanted weapon has certainly proven
useful on screen for both combat and for just

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:49.260
getting around, and Hemsworth has apparently
taken a huge liking to it in real life, bringing

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.940
several of the prop hammers home with him
after wrapping films in the MCU.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.300
While the Aussie actor loves having them around,
his wife, model and actress Elsa Pataky, has

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:03.140
reached her limit on the prop in their home,
so much so that she's imposed a strict rule:

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.140
Hemsworth absolutely has to quit swiping hammers
from set.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:10.740
Speaking on the Australian radio show Fitzy
and Wippa, Pataky shared that her husband

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.660
has snatched not just one prop Mjolnir...

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.060
"How many hammers do you have?"

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:15.640
"Uhhh… about five?"

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.400
"Five hammers!"

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:21.960
Now, don't get us wrong Mjolnir is an epic
weapon to wield, but that's an awful lot of

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.119
hammers for people in the house to trip over.

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:28.369
Especially considering, y'know, some mere
mortal can't just lift it up and move it over

00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:31.740
a few inches unless they're also wielding
America's ass, that is.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.360
Yeah, you know who we're talking about.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:38.140
Jokes aside, Pataky also explained that she
and Hemsworth have regular arguments over

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:40.600
where the props are and aren't allowed to
go in the house.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.300
She dished:

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.200
"He always picks the best places in the house,
and I'm like, 'It's not going there.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.760
We have five of them [ … ] like, seriously,
no."

00:01:48.009 --> 00:01:52.520
Of course, Thor would want his trusty Mjolnir
close at hand at all times, so Hemsworth wants

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:57.070
to make sure the hammers are prominently displayed
all over the couple's Australian home in case

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:00.260
of emergency or maybe in case he needs a last-minute
gift.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.620
Remind us which year is the "enchanted Asgardian
hammer" anniversary?

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:08.229
We also can't imagine Pataky would have been
any happier if her husband brought home Thor's

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:09.000
second weapon.

00:02:09.289 --> 00:02:14.080
Stormbreaker the giant battle axe Thor helps
forge after his sister Hela destroys Mjolnir

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:18.650
in Thor: Ragnarok is just a tad bigger than
the hammer, so here's hoping Pataky hasn't

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.020
had to find a space for this significantly
larger weapon in the house.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:27.120
Unfortunately for Pataky, the flow of hammers
isn't likely to stop flowing anytime soon,

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:27.920
despite her ban.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:32.400
Hemsworth is set to appear as Thor again in
Thor: Love and Thunder, which is set for release

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.960
in November 2021.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:38.380
Though Pataky has put her foot down and warned
him not to bring more hammers home, Hemsworth

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:42.799
seems like the cheeky type who might want
just one extra prop, and Pataky just might

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.100
have to find space for more of her husband's
very unique brand of decor.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:50.900
Thor: Love and Thunder will see a new hero
rise up to take the mantle and powers of Thor:

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.209
the God of Thunder's former love interest,
Jane Foster played by Natalie Portman is set

00:02:55.209 --> 00:03:00.401
to make a return to the MCU after seemingly
quitting for good following 2013's Thor: The

00:03:00.401 --> 00:03:01.080
Dark World.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:05.600
In the upcoming flick, fans will get to see
Jane wield Mjolnir when she becomes the Mighty

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:06.100
Thor.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:10.160
Hopefully for Pataky, Portman will be the
one taking the hammer home this time around.

